[{:db/id 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a68b0724-2e6f-5527-bb88-98de4c797f20" "question-d48bb18b-a23a-5640-ba69-c0db05f527bc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e525b492-a29a-585f-8c96-2055a51f2341"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a68b0724-2e6f-5527-bb88-98de4c797f20" :question/id #uuid "a68b0724-2e6f-5527-bb88-98de4c797f20" :question/math-academy-id "q-81010" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & x+2y\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & x+2y\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x+2y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+2y)=1 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=1\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+2y)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1e2c894b-e18f-5a60-9da4-9f38bca23df7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e2c894b-e18f-5a60-9da4-9f38bca23df7" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e2c894b-e18f-5a60-9da4-9f38bca23df7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-986935ae-ac9e-5393-98ba-0d529a02cf04" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35addae1-944d-5e96-bf7b-9d53283e50fa" "answer-0eed068e-354b-5c24-8218-ac1367acc3ab" "answer-8923009c-c530-5063-8998-6977d181f503" "answer-428be636-82c8-5886-b28a-43069f19e0f2" "answer-986935ae-ac9e-5393-98ba-0d529a02cf04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35addae1-944d-5e96-bf7b-9d53283e50fa" :answer/id #uuid "35addae1-944d-5e96-bf7b-9d53283e50fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & y \\\\ y & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0eed068e-354b-5c24-8218-ac1367acc3ab" :answer/id #uuid "0eed068e-354b-5c24-8218-ac1367acc3ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8923009c-c530-5063-8998-6977d181f503" :answer/id #uuid "8923009c-c530-5063-8998-6977d181f503" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-428be636-82c8-5886-b28a-43069f19e0f2" :answer/id #uuid "428be636-82c8-5886-b28a-43069f19e0f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-986935ae-ac9e-5393-98ba-0d529a02cf04" :answer/id #uuid "986935ae-ac9e-5393-98ba-0d529a02cf04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d48bb18b-a23a-5640-ba69-c0db05f527bc" :question/id #uuid "d48bb18b-a23a-5640-ba69-c0db05f527bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-102452" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(2,1)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-2xy & 2y-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-2xy & 2y-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}],$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2xy)=-2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-{x}^{2})=-2x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2xy)=-2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y-{x}^{2})=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2y & -2x \\\\ -2x & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(2,1).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(2,1)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e0eb9da-e4d5-55d6-ad33-7db8760cccce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e0eb9da-e4d5-55d6-ad33-7db8760cccce" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e0eb9da-e4d5-55d6-ad33-7db8760cccce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-afde4582-cdac-5bc3-b210-1397789ef534" :answer-field/choices ["answer-533319f1-cf66-5e55-a50b-27c89a39ea11" "answer-afde4582-cdac-5bc3-b210-1397789ef534" "answer-3f5dbce3-5eeb-5299-a81b-71b95b40a702" "answer-ef6b5589-dee3-5358-89b2-bb7e5109233c" "answer-f224da51-5558-5714-9c8e-ab71238f6195"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-533319f1-cf66-5e55-a50b-27c89a39ea11" :answer/id #uuid "533319f1-cf66-5e55-a50b-27c89a39ea11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afde4582-cdac-5bc3-b210-1397789ef534" :answer/id #uuid "afde4582-cdac-5bc3-b210-1397789ef534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f5dbce3-5eeb-5299-a81b-71b95b40a702" :answer/id #uuid "3f5dbce3-5eeb-5299-a81b-71b95b40a702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef6b5589-dee3-5358-89b2-bb7e5109233c" :answer/id #uuid "ef6b5589-dee3-5358-89b2-bb7e5109233c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f224da51-5558-5714-9c8e-ab71238f6195" :answer/id #uuid "f224da51-5558-5714-9c8e-ab71238f6195" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e525b492-a29a-585f-8c96-2055a51f2341" :question/id #uuid "e525b492-a29a-585f-8c96-2055a51f2341" :question/math-academy-id "q-102686" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{2} & 2y{x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{2} & 2y{x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y{x}^{2}-1)=4xy \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2})=4xy\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{x}^{2}-1)=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,-1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,-1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,-1)=2\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=-12.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-835cf471-5984-50ad-ac7a-5c92395f40c6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-835cf471-5984-50ad-ac7a-5c92395f40c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "835cf471-5984-50ad-ac7a-5c92395f40c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-012e8862-6d84-5ca3-808d-e580b5b68412" :answer-field/choices ["answer-012e8862-6d84-5ca3-808d-e580b5b68412" "answer-1d97894b-06e8-5458-afce-3b6280583bcd" "answer-6341ade3-f46e-594c-b2db-483df7d6f5cd" "answer-49af7f88-d313-53b2-a836-26eef4f823e6" "answer-e9393f5b-f485-5c2a-b52d-4ac15221029b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-012e8862-6d84-5ca3-808d-e580b5b68412" :answer/id #uuid "012e8862-6d84-5ca3-808d-e580b5b68412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d97894b-06e8-5458-afce-3b6280583bcd" :answer/id #uuid "1d97894b-06e8-5458-afce-3b6280583bcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6341ade3-f46e-594c-b2db-483df7d6f5cd" :answer/id #uuid "6341ade3-f46e-594c-b2db-483df7d6f5cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49af7f88-d313-53b2-a836-26eef4f823e6" :answer/id #uuid "49af7f88-d313-53b2-a836-26eef4f823e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9393f5b-f485-5c2a-b52d-4ac15